...@_house

# Grid drops edges between cells, so the gate points at cards by name.
grid-rows: 3
grid-columns: 1
grid-gap: 60

gate: "CONCEPT GATE  ::  yes moves down, no exits right to a card below" {
  class: stage

  (* -> *)[*].style.stroke-width: 6
  (* -> *)[*].style.font-size: 28
  (* -> *)[*].style.bold: true

  q1: "the frontier defect,\nand why 420 fixtures graded IDENTICAL?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c1: "no: CARD 1" {class: muted}
  q1 -> c1: no

  q2: "why does the supportSql rename\nmove 747 emitted modules?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c2: "no: CARD 2" {class: muted}
  q1 -> q2: yes
  q2 -> c2: no

  q3: "what does unreadRels skip,\nwhat would cone-deriving it change?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c3: "no: CARD 3" {class: muted}
  q2 -> q3: yes
  q3 -> c3: no

  q4: "who consumes the tick log,\nwhat breaks if SQL builds the line?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c4: "no: CARD 4" {class: muted}
  q3 -> q4: yes
  q4 -> c4: no

  q5: "why does retraction on a recursive head\nwork TODAY?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: danger
  }
  c5: "no: CARD 5,\nthe one design question" {class: muted}
  q4 -> q5: yes
  q5 -> c5: no

  q6: "which sweep stage fails,\nwhose defect?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c6: "no: CARD 6" {class: muted}
  q5 -> q6: yes
  q6 -> c6: no

  q7: "why is worktree removal\nyours to run?" {
    shape: diamond
    class: designed
  }
  c7: "no: CARD 7" {class: muted}
  q6 -> q7: yes
  q7 -> c7: no

  done: "all concepts held:\ndecide in the order below" {class: chosen}
  q7 -> done: yes
}

order: |||md
  ## decide in this order
  | order | decision | why this slot |
  |---|---|---|
  | 1 | merge PR #7 | everything below sits on its head |
  | 2 | rename word | own commit ON TOP of the merge, never inside it |
  | 3 | card 5 design call | largest remaining structural cost, 63% of tick |
  | 4 | cards 3 + 4 together | both trade marshalling against the tick log oracle |
  | 5 | dispatch card 6 | independent defect, flash4 lane |
  | 6 | run card 7 yourself | one command, blocked for agents |
||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}

items: "THE SEVEN CARDS" {
  class: stage
  grid-rows: 7
  grid-columns: 1
  grid-gap: 40

  card1: "1. PR #7 merge  ::  READY, nothing blocked" {
    class: stage
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | number |
      |---|---|
      | commits on `lab/emit-reconcile` | 21, head 39ae7072, base e3997cec |
      | ladder | 106,692 ms -> 2,200 ms (38.4x), 1.98 GB -> 724 MB |
      | defect A | closure loop re-read the whole frontier every round, ONE DAY old |
      | defect B | every derived row round-tripped through JS, twice through JSON |
      | why no gate saw A | sweep grades END STATE; a naive closure ends identical |
      | the rail that now sees it | recursiveClosureCounts.test.ts, 39/59/91 pre-fix vs 36/36/36 |
      | gates | tsv2 146/1skip, conformance 302/0, sweep 420 byte-identical |
    ||| {class: shipped; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      merge as-is / read the PR body first / hold.
      Cards 2..5 all assume this lands first.
    ||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card2: "2. supportSql -> refCountSql  ::  LAW VIOLATION, awaiting word" {
    class: danger
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | where |
      |---|---|
      | the law: "support" is banned, use refCount | CLAUDE.md:78, rename recorded as EXECUTED 2026-08-02 |
      | survivors | 1_incremental.ts x7, lower.pl x1 (`__support_next_~w`), types.ts, 3 test files |
      | also survivors | every emitted module + all of gen_served/ |
      | comments already say refCount | lower.pl:1857 |
      | correct names | `refCountSql`, `__ref_next_<rel>` |
      | why 747 modules move | the string is INSIDE the emitted SQL, so every module's text changes |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      when, never whether. Own commit, sweep as the gate,
      on top of the merge so PR #7's diff stays readable.
    ||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card3: "3. unreadRels  ::  opt-in today, general version changes the log" {
    class: stage
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | number |
      |---|---|
      | what it does | a rel nobody reads keeps its rows in SQLite, readBoundary skips it |
      | measured win | gate 2 went 6,148 -> 2,825 ms, RSS 1.64 GB -> 978 MB |
      | who declares it | only the dl6 entrant, by hand, per caller |
      | the general version | derive the set from the subscription cone |
      | its cost | the observable tick log changes, so the 420-log oracle re-baselines |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      keep opt-in (safe, manual) / derive from the cone
      (general, re-baseline) / cone-derived but behind a flag.
      Decide together with card 4: same oracle at risk.
    ||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card4: "4. tick log built in SQL  ::  last ~33% of marshalling" {
    class: stage
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | number |
      |---|---|
      | today | readBoundary materializes every row as a JS object to print a line |
      | cost per row | ~140 bytes as a JS object vs ~20 as a btree entry |
      | the idea | `group_concat` builds the log line inside SQLite |
      | who it helps | callers that DO read; unreadRels already covers the rest |
      | the risk | 420 byte-identical tick logs are the sweep's oracle |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      do it and prove byte-identity per fixture / skip until a
      caller is measured to need it. Decide with card 3.
    ||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card5: "5. recursive CTE recompute  ::  THE design question" {
    class: danger
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | where |
      |---|---|
      | supportSql reseeds the closure FROM SCRATCH every tick | 1_incremental.ts:819 path |
      | share of tick | 63% after all optimization, priced 1,420 ms on the probe |
      | the law it trips | recompute-guard: from-scratch re-derive needs a digest early-out or a waiver |
      | why retraction works today | ONLY because the recompute is full: rebuild forgets retracted rows for free |
      | refCount on a recursive head | presence, never a derivation count: lower.pl:2486 seeds `SELECT cols, 1` under a deduping UNION |
      | so a semi-naive CTE | must solve retraction some OTHER way, counting is not there to lean on |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      digest early-out (cheap, keeps full recompute on change) /
      `@recompute unguarded` waiver (declare it intended) /
      semi-naive seeding (largest win, must re-solve retraction).
    ||| {class: chosen; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card6: "6. sweep stage 4 duplicate manifest  ::  dispatchable" {
    class: stage
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | detail |
      |---|---|
      | fixture | `enum_decl_variant_rows_round_trip_through_tag_view` |
      | symptom | duplicate manifest row that HEAD's manifest does not carry |
      | fixture source | defines the row ONCE, so the generator invents the duplicate |
      | blast radius | generator only, engine untouched, no other stage red |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the choice
      dispatch to a flash4 lane with the fixture name and the
      manifest diff as the receipt, or park. Blocks nothing.
    ||| {class: muted; shape: rectangle}
  }

  card7: "7. worktree cleanup  ::  yours to run" {
    class: stage
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 20

    ctx: |||md
      ## prior context
      | fact | detail |
      |---|---|
      | count | 21+ stale worktrees under ~/projects/sprefa-lanes |
      | why agents cannot | `git worktree remove` is blocked by the permission classifier |
      | keep alive | `emitrace` (PR #7 head) and `sprefa-types` (64c77bb4, in-flight) |
    ||| {class: src; shape: rectangle}

    choice: |||md
      ## the command
      `git worktree list`, then `git worktree remove <path>`
      per stale tree, `git worktree prune` last.
    ||| {class: muted; shape: rectangle}
  }
}
